<title>INDIA: TABLE-India Ashok 96/97 net up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-India Ashok 96/97 net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	  1,249.33     vs	 1,130.83</p>
<p>    Net sales	  24,901.44     vs	20,158.05</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	 5.00     vs	     4.00</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	10.50     vs	     9.51</p>
<p>    Expenditure	22,573.41     vs	18,639.43</p>
<p>    Gross Operating   2,328.03     vs	 1,518.62</p>
<p>Margin</p>
<p>    Other income	  182.62     vs	   145.77</p>
<p>    Interest		284.34     vs	  (217.49)</p>
<p>    Gross Profit	2,226.31     vs	 1,881.88</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  655.98     vs	   546.05</p>
<p>    Tax		     321.00     vs	   205.00</p>
<p>Note: Ashok Leyland Ltd. is India's second largest truckmaker. It said that despite a sluggish market, the firm's 96/97 vehicle production rose 18 percent, with sales up 16 percent, over last year's figures.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom =91-22-265 9000</p>
